4. **`value_to_f64`** — `#[no_mangle]` + `extern "C"` for stable C linkage; the null-check returns `-1` *before* anything is dereferenced; `VAL_INT` performs the numeric `i64 -> f64` conversion (so e.g. `3` becomes `3.0`); `VAL_FLOAT` copies the float; `VAL_BYTES` → `-2`; any other tag → `-3`. In the two error cases after the null check (`-2`, `-3`), `*out` is never written, preserving the "left untouched" guarantee; on success (`0`) `*out` is the only thing written.

